      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\n\nLocation: Sioux City\n\nAssistant/Associate Professor - Chemistry The Department of Biology and Chemistry and the Chemistry program at Briar Cliff University seek to fill an Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry position to begin in Spring 2027 (preferred) or Fall 2027. This is a 9-month, tenure-eligible position focused on advancing knowledge through teaching, professional development, and service within the university community.  The successful candidate will teach courses in beginning and advanced chemistry, chemical engineering, and/or other courses that serve the University’s general education curriculum, known as the Core Values Curriculum. The typical faculty teaching load is 24 credits over the normal academic year. Collaboration with colleagues across departments and programs, and participation in curriculum development are essential to ensure the academic program remains current and rigorous. Additionally, faculty engage in professional development, complete institutional and departmental service, and advise students regarding experiential learning opportunities in addition to their coursework, supporting their professional growth and contributing to the broader educational mission.  The successful candidate should have a Ph.D. in Chemistry or related field. Exceptional ABD candidates will also be considered, and the candidate must have their degree completed no later than the end of their second year in the position. The successful candidate should demonstrate excellence in teaching at the university level, a strong record of successfully advising and mentoring students, an interest in maintaining their own intellectual creativity, and an ability to contribute to curriculum development and academic service.  Founded in 1930 and rooted in the Catholic Franciscan tradition, Briar Cliff University is a vibrant, values-based community dedicated to academic excellence and personal growth. Located on the sceni